<title>JAPAN: Portugal launches 4.95% yen/dlr samurai - Nomura.</title>
<headline>Portugal launches 4.95% yen/dlr samurai - Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Republic of Portugal</p>
<p> AMT		 30 billion yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.95 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  31 Jan 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  30 Jan 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Jan 20 to Jan 28</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's A1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Sanwa Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,275.33 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
